{
  "rules": [
    "Persistent positive bias: forecasts are systematically too high vs realized prices, especially from ~day 8 onward; apply a downward level shift (bias correction) that increases with horizon.",
    "Trend/mean-reversion miss in downtrends: when the last 30d history is falling, the model reverts upward too quickly and too strongly; dampen mean-reversion strength and allow continued drift lower.",
    "Horizon-dependent overshoot: long-horizon (≈day 15–30) forecasts overshoot most, often by ~5–12 EUR; use a horizon ramp correction (small cut for days 1–5, larger cut for days 10–30).",
    "Lag/underreaction to regime change: after a break lower, the model stays anchored to prior higher levels; incorporate a stronger weight on the most recent 5–10 days (or add a regime-shift detector) to pull the whole path down faster.",
    "Volatility/spike handling: after short-term upticks in history, the model extrapolates rebounds that do not materialize; cap rebound amplitude and enforce asymmetric response (down moves persist longer than up moves in this sample)."
  ]
}
